
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Apple&#8217;s Live Rewind feature has made it into the watchOS 27.3 developer beta. I know there&#8217;s a lot of consternation about this feature, but I&#8217;m a fan. Let me explain.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I have significant hearing loss. I think it&#8217;s primarily because I played in so many bands when I was young, but for whatever reason, my hearing ain&#8217;t so good. Several years ago, I got hearing aids, and they help a great deal, but technology can only help so much.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And often when I&#8217;m out, particularly in public places where there&#8217;s a lot of background noise, I have a hard time understanding what people are saying to me. My family&#8217;s kind of used to me asking them to repeat themselves.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">But I can tell you, when you ask a stranger to repeat themselves a couple times, they get really annoyed. So often, to avoid the awkwardness, I just nod my head yes and hope that whatever I just agreed to didn&#8217;t involve sacrificing a kidney.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">So I, for one, am really looking forward to having Live Rewind on my wrist, where I can subtly read what was just said to me without making a big deal of it. I&#8217;ve just installed the beta on my phone, and I&#8217;m just starting to test the feature, and I don&#8217;t have an opinion on it yet.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">But I do want this to be a thing.</p>
